WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.636 --> 00:00:21.135
As the church clock struck two, Jean Valjean awoke in the bishop's house.

2
00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:29.547
Many thoughts passed through his mind, but one kept returning: there was a small fortune in silver in the next room!

3
00:00:29.548 --> 00:00:35.785
The six plates and the ladle were worth twice what he had earned for 19 years of prison labor.

4
00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:40.630
Valjean sat on the edge of the bed, thinking about the silver for an hour.

5
00:00:40.631 --> 00:00:44.531
He might have remained there longer if the clock hadn't struck again.

6
00:00:44.532 --> 00:00:54.690
The clock seemed to say, "Let's go!" So Valjean stood up and went to the door that led to the bishop's bedroom. The bishop had left it ajar.

7
00:00:54.691 --> 00:01:00.102
Valjean pushed the door lightly with his fingertip, and it opened a little wider.

8
00:01:00.103 --> 00:01:05.665
He waited a moment and then pushed the door again, more boldly this time.

9
00:01:05.666 --> 00:01:12.086
The door opened wide with a loud creak. Valjean froze with his heart pounding.

10
00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:14.298
But no one in the house woke up.

11
00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:22.237
Valjean peered into the room and saw the bishop sleeping peacefully, a beam of moonlight illuminating his pale face.

12
00:01:22.238 --> 00:01:25.300
Valjean slipped silently into the room.

13
00:01:25.302 --> 00:01:31.332
He opened the cupboard at the head of the bed and removed the basket containing the ladle and plates.

14
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:38.229
Once outside he threw away the basket, ran across the garden, and leaped over the low, white wall.

15
00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:44.554
The next morning the bishop was walking in the garden when his housekeeper dashed out of the house.

16
00:01:44.555 --> 00:01:49.141
"The silver basket has disappeared!" cried Madame Magloire.

17
00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:54.483
"I just found it here in the garden." The bishop calmly handed the basket to her.

18
00:01:54.484 --> 00:02:00.221
"But there's nothing in it! That man who came last night must have stolen the silver."

19
00:02:00.222 --> 00:02:09.284
Madame Magloire ran back into the bishop's house while he bent sadly over a flower lying on the ground. The basket had broken its stem.

20
00:02:09.285 --> 00:02:16.205
Madame Magloire came running into the garden again. "He's gone!" she said to the bishop.

21
00:02:16.206 --> 00:02:24.689
The bishop was silent for a moment. Then he said, "I held on to that silver for a long time when I should have given it to the poor.

22
00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:30.935
Our visitor was evidently a poor man, so it's appropriate that the silver now belongs to him."

23
00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:35.197
"But what are you going to eat from? We don't have any—"

24
00:02:35.198 --> 00:02:39.917
Their discussion was interrupted by the bishop's sister calling to them from a window.

25
00:02:39.918 --> 00:02:44.697
"Someone's knocking at the front door!" cried Mademoiselle Baptistine.

26
00:02:44.698 --> 00:02:49.927
Madame Magloire hurried into the house with the bishop following slowly behind her.

27
00:02:49.928 --> 00:02:53.491
"Come in!" said the bishop when he reached the front room.

28
00:02:53.492 --> 00:03:01.166
The door opened and there stood three policemen. One held Jean Valjean by his collar.

29
00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:08.816
"I'm so happy to see you again," the bishop said kindly to Valjean. "I meant for you to have my candlesticks too.

30
00:03:08.817 --> 00:03:15.499
Why didn't you take them along with your ladle and plates? They're also made of silver and will bring a good price."

31
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.904
Valjean's eyes widened, and he looked at the bishop with a stunned expression.

32
00:03:20.905 --> 00:03:27.396
"He seemed to be running away from something," said one of the policemen. "So we stopped him and found your silver."

33
00:03:27.397 --> 00:03:31.655
"And then I'm sure he told you that he'd spent the night here and that I'd given it to him.

34
00:03:31.656 --> 00:03:34.983
I hope you can see that you've made a terrible mistake."

35
00:03:34.984 --> 00:03:39.555
"If that's the truth, then we'll let him go," said the same policeman.

36
00:03:39.556 --> 00:03:47.447
"Let him go," said the bishop. Then he went to the mantel, picked up the two candlesticks, and handed them to Valjean.

37
00:03:47.448 --> 00:03:50.199
"Here are your candlesticks, my friend."

38
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.541
Madame Magloire and Mademoiselle Baptistine were too amazed to speak.

39
00:03:55.542 --> 00:03:59.795
Valjean took the candlesticks with a wild look in his eye.

40
00:03:59.796 --> 00:04:06.194
"By the way, my friend," continued the bishop, "the next time you visit, you don't have to come through the garden.

41
00:04:06.195 --> 00:04:10.946
You can always come in by the front door; it's never locked."

42
00:04:10.947 --> 00:04:15.858
The policemen left, and the bishop turned his attention to Valjean again.

43
00:04:15.859 --> 00:04:26.192
In a quiet voice he said, "Never forget that you've promised me to use this silver to become an honest man. Now go in peace."

44
00:04:26.193 --> 00:04:32.438
Valjean knew that he hadn't promised the bishop anything, but he was too astonished to say a word.

45
00:04:32.439 --> 00:04:40.415
He fled from the bishop's house and the town as fast as he could. Valjean felt angry, but he wasn't sure with whom.

46
00:04:40.416 --> 00:04:46.256
He didn't know whether he should feel touched—or humiliated—by the bishop's actions.

47
00:04:46.257 --> 00:04:52.820
Perhaps he would be less agitated if the police had taken him to prison. At least he knew how to deal with prison!

48
00:04:52.821 --> 00:04:59.502
As the sun was setting, Valjean sat by the side of the road only a few miles from the bishop's house.

49
00:04:59.503 --> 00:05:05.058
He had been wandering and thinking all day without paying attention to where he was going.

50
00:05:05.059 --> 00:05:09.399
In a few minutes, a young chimney sweep came walking down the road.

51
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:18.161
The boy was busy singing and tossing a handful of coins in the air. He had managed to catch them all on the back of his hand. Until now.

52
00:05:18.162 --> 00:05:26.883
A silver forty-sou coin got away from him and rolled toward the man sitting by the road. Valjean promptly put his foot on top of it.

53
00:05:26.884 --> 00:05:31.001
The boy walked over to him and said, "Monsieur, give me my coin."

54
00:05:31.002 --> 00:05:32.621
"What's your name?"

55
00:05:32.622 --> 00:05:34.028
"Little Gervais."

56
00:05:34.029 --> 00:05:38.216
"Go away, Little Gervais," said Valjean, looking at the ground.

57
00:05:38.217 --> 00:05:42.962
The boy repeated his request, and Valjean continued to look at the ground.

58
00:05:42.963 --> 00:05:51.367
Little Gervais tried to move the big, heavy-soled shoe that covered his treasure. The child began to cry, and Valjean looked up.

59
00:05:51.368 --> 00:05:57.938
"Are you still here?" Valjean said in a menacing voice. He stood up suddenly without moving his foot.

60
00:05:57.939 --> 00:06:01.184
"You'd better get going if you know what's good for you."

61
00:06:01.185 --> 00:06:05.208
The boy looked at him in terror before running away as fast as possible.

62
00:06:05.209 --> 00:06:10.430
A few minutes later, Valjean heard him sobbing, and then there was silence.

63
00:06:10.431 --> 00:06:17.763
Valjean continued to sit by the side of the road until it was dark. When he stood up again, he saw the coin.

64
00:06:17.764 --> 00:06:24.256
"What's this?" he said to himself, and then he remembered the chimney sweep. "I've done a bad thing.

65
00:06:24.257 --> 00:06:27.263
I must find that boy and return this to him."

66
00:06:27.264 --> 00:06:33.232
Valjean called the boy's name over and over again, but there was no response.

67
00:06:33.233 --> 00:06:37.073
He started to walk and soon met a priest on horseback.

68
00:06:37.074 --> 00:06:42.840
"Father, have you passed a boy on the road?" asked Valjean. "He's about 12 years old."

69
00:06:42.841 --> 00:06:45.756
"I've seen no one," said the priest.

70
00:06:45.757 --> 00:06:52.484
"Here," said Valjean, handing the priest a few coins. "Take these and give them to the poor in your parish."

71
00:06:52.485 --> 00:06:57.065
Then he added, "I'm a robber, and you should have me arrested."

72
00:06:57.066 --> 00:06:59.082
The priest fled in fear.

73
00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:02.319
For hours Valjean kept searching for Little Gervais.

74
00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:10.144
Suddenly his knees buckled and he fell to the ground. It was as if the weight of his guilty conscience had overwhelmed him.

75
00:07:10.145 --> 00:07:17.446
"What a wretch I am!" he exclaimed, and he burst into tears for the first time in 19 years.

76
00:07:17.447 --> 00:07:20.278
Valjean realized that he had to change.

77
00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:26.644
When the church clock chimed three on that morning, he was kneeling in prayer at the bishop's door.
